<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Zhuyin (注音 / Bopomofo) layout: ㄅㄆㄇㄈ symbols are the primary key labels;
    long-press popups follow the Boshiamy convention: symbol-first, then the
    fullwidth Latin letter, then extra Bopomofo. Codes are Bopomofo Unicode
    codepoints (U+3105..U+3129, plus tone marks U+02C7/02CA/02CB/02D9) so that
    the radical buffer accumulates Bopomofo syllables which can then be looked
    up in zhuyin_radicals.

    Mapping follows the standard 大千 (Dachen) Bopomofo keyboard layout.
    The top row is the row that on a US-QWERTY keyboard holds the digit row;
    in 大千 it carries ㄅ ㄉ ˇ ˋ ㄓ ˊ ˙ ㄚ ㄞ ㄢ; the digits themselves remain
    available via long-press.

    Zhuyin has no concept of shift, so there is no shift key on the bottom
    row; the freed width goes to the additional Bopomofo letters
    ㄝ ㄡ ㄥ ㄦ that would otherwise be hidden in popups.

    autoCap is disabled because Bopomofo radicals are single-character labels;
    auto-cap would otherwise shift the keyboard view and (for theme renderers
    that fall back to the key code) display the underlying numeric codes.
-->
<Keyboard xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:ask="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res-auto"
    android:keyWidth="10%p"
    android:keyHeight="@integer/key_normal_height"
    ask:autoCap="false">

